@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-registrar`
IMPORT `g4-council-membership`
IMPORT `g4-council-work`
IMPORT `g4-conflict`
IMPORT `g4-composition`

-- ind-b-tests-g4.l4: INDEPENDENT tests (author ind-b) of ss.19 to 29 (the Registrar and the Council).
-- Every expected value comes from work/ind-b/expectations.md, written from the sources BEFORE the encoding
-- was opened; the scenario id is given beside each assertion.  Inputs the encoding needs that a scenario does
-- not state (a judgement, an opinion) are supplied as stated assumptions in the fixture.  Nothing here was
-- edited to match the code; failing assertions live in ind-b-tests-disagree.l4 and ind-b-tests-ambiguous.l4.

§ `ind-b: independent tests of sections 19 to 29`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN isAppointed IS A BOOLEAN, isEmployee IS A BOOLEAN, isPublished IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Appointment of a Registrar`
`ind-b appointment: by the Minister` isAppointed `, Ministry employee` isEmployee `, notice published` isPublished MEANS
    `Appointment of a Registrar` WITH
        `the Minister appointed the person` IS isAppointed
        `the person is an employee of the Ministry` IS isEmployee
        `notice of the appointment was published in Reshumot` IS isPublished

GIVEN hasConsent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Study programme under section 19(b)`
`ind-b a programme leading to a final certificate, consent given` hasConsent MEANS
    `Study programme under section 19(b)` WITH
        `the programme` IS "an evening course in refrigeration"
        `a final certificate as stated in section 6(a)(4) can be obtained through the programme` IS TRUE
        `the Registrar consented to the programme` IS hasConsent

GIVEN matches IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)`
`ind-b a foreign diploma whose scope and content match` matches MEANS
    `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` WITH
        `a description of the qualification` IS "a diploma in refrigeration from a college abroad"
        `a certificate, degree or training from an educational institution in a foreign country` IS TRUE
        `in the Registrar's opinion the scope and content of the studies match the training requirements of section 6(a)(4)` IS matches
        `the Registrar recognised the qualification as meeting the training and examination requirements for a licence` IS TRUE
        `the Registrar made the recognition conditional on a test, training or both` IS TRUE
        `the condition of the recognition was met` IS TRUE

GIVETH A `Matters the Registrar considered under section 19(c)(2)`
`ind-b all four matters considered` MEANS
    `Matters the Registrar considered under section 19(c)(2)` WITH
        `the level of the studies, compared with the level customary at institutions the Training Division recognises` IS TRUE
        `the programme of the studies, compared with the programme customary at institutions the Training Division recognises` IS TRUE
        `the scope of the studies, compared with the scope customary at institutions the Training Division recognises` IS TRUE
        `the duration of the studies, compared with the duration customary at institutions the Training Division recognises` IS TRUE

GIVEN isUnfit IS A BOOLEAN, outcome IS AN `Outcome of a proceeding against a Council candidate or member`
GIVETH A `Proceeding against a Council candidate or member for an offence`
`ind-b a proceeding, unfitting` isUnfit `, ending` outcome MEANS
    `Proceeding against a Council candidate or member for an offence` WITH
        `the offence, by its nature, severity or circumstances, makes the person unfit to be a member of the Council` IS isUnfit
        `the outcome of the proceeding` IS outcome

GIVEN holds IS A BOOLEAN, proposed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Candidate for a seat on the Council`
`ind-b a candidate holding the position` holds `, proposed by the competent Minister` proposed MEANS
    `Candidate for a seat on the Council` WITH
        `holds the position the seat describes` IS holds
        `the competent Minister or Commissioner proposed the appointment` IS proposed
        `in the Minister's opinion the candidate or the candidate's organisation is as the seat describes` IS TRUE
        `is a practical engineer or an engineer` IS FALSE

GIVETH AN `Events ending a member's service under section 23(a)`
`ind-b no events` MEANS
    `Events ending a member's service under section 23(a)` WITH
        `the day the member delivered a letter of resignation to the Minister` IS NOTHING
        `the day the member ceased to be an employee of the government ministry or a member of the body the member represents` IS NOTHING
        `the day the member, a public representative, was appointed a State employee` IS NOTHING

GIVEN ref IS A STRING, seat IS A `Council seat`
GIVETH A `Service record of a member of the Council`
`ind-b a record for` ref `in` seat `appointed 1.3.2025` MEANS
    `Service record of a member of the Council` WITH
        `reference for the member` IS ref
        `the seat` IS seat
        `appointed on` IS YMD 2025 3 1
        `further terms granted by the Minister` IS 0
        `events ending service under section 23(a)` IS `ind-b no events`
        `removed from office by the Minister on` IS NOTHING

GIVETH A LIST OF `Service record of a member of the Council`
`ind-b eleven records appointed 1.3.2025` MEANS
    LIST `ind-b a record for` "s1" `in` `seat 1: representative of the senior occupations-regulation division of the Ministry, the chair` `appointed 1.3.2025`
       , `ind-b a record for` "s2" `in` `seat 2: the Registrar` `appointed 1.3.2025`
       , `ind-b a record for` "s3" `in` `seat 3: the Commissioner for Standards, or an employee on the Commissioner's behalf` `appointed 1.3.2025`
       , `ind-b a record for` "s4" `in` `seat 4: employee of the Ministry of Energy and Infrastructure` `appointed 1.3.2025`
       , `ind-b a record for` "s5" `in` `seat 5: employee of the Ministry of Environmental Protection` `appointed 1.3.2025`
       , `ind-b a record for` "s6" `in` `seat 6: employee of the National Fire and Rescue Authority` `appointed 1.3.2025`
       , `ind-b a record for` "s7" `in` `seat 7: representative of the workers' organisation with the most licence holders` `appointed 1.3.2025`
       , `ind-b a record for` "s8" `in` `seat 8: representative of an employers' organisation` `appointed 1.3.2025`
       , `ind-b a record for` "s9" `in` `seat 9: representative of the organisation with the most engineers` `appointed 1.3.2025`
       , `ind-b a record for` "s10" `in` `seat 10: representative of the representative organisation under the Engineers and Technicians Law` `appointed 1.3.2025`
       , `ind-b a record for` "s11" `in` `seat 11: public representative` `appointed 1.3.2025`

GIVEN procs IS A LIST OF `Proceeding against a Council candidate or member for an offence`
      unable IS A BOOLEAN
      satisfies IS A BOOLEAN
      barred IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about a member for section 23(b)`
`ind-b member facts: proceedings` procs `, permanently unable` unable `, still meets the seat` satisfies `, barred by 29(b)` barred MEANS
    `Facts about a member for section 23(b)` WITH
        `the proceedings against the member` IS procs
        `the member is permanently unable to perform the function` IS unable
        `the member still satisfies the conditions of the seat` IS satisfies
        `the member is barred from the Council by section 29(b)` IS barred
        `the member has not already ceased to serve under section 23(a)` IS TRUE

-- s.23(c): one meeting a month on the 10th of 2026, coded "A" attended, "U" absent without justification,
-- "J" absent with justification; the member serving throughout; Council meetings, not a subcommittee's.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, att IS A BOOLEAN, just IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance`
`ind-b meeting on` d `, attended` att `, justified` just MEANS
    `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance` WITH
        `the day of the meeting` IS d
        `held by a subcommittee of the Council` IS FALSE
        `the member was serving on the day of the meeting` IS TRUE
        `the member attended` IS att
        `the absence was justified` IS just

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, codes IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF `Meeting of the Council and a member's attendance`
`ind-b meetings of 2026 from month` m `coded` codes MEANS
    CONSIDER codes
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (`ind-b meeting on` (YMD 2026 m 10) `, attended` (c EQUALS "A") `, justified` (c EQUALS "J"))
        FOLLOWED BY (`ind-b meetings of 2026 from month` (m PLUS 1) `coded` rest)

GIVEN codes IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-b ground under s 23(c) on 1.11.2026 for` codes MEANS
    `s 23(c) — a ground for removal by absence exists on` (YMD 2026 11 1) `, according to` (`ind-b meetings of 2026 from month` 1 `coded` codes)

-- s.24, s.25: eleven serving members m1 .. m11, m1 holding the chair's seat.
GIVEN ref IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Serving member of the Council`
`ind-b serving member` ref MEANS
    `Serving member of the Council` WITH
        `reference for the member` IS ref
        `the member is the chair` IS ref EQUALS "m1"

GIVEN refs IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF `Serving member of the Council`
`ind-b serving` refs MEANS
    map (GIVEN r YIELD `ind-b serving member` r) refs

GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`ind-b all eleven` MEANS
    LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6", "m7", "m8", "m9", "m10", "m11"

GIVEN serving IS A LIST OF STRING
      summoned IS A BOOLEAN
      present IS A LIST OF STRING
      votesFor IS A LIST OF STRING
      votesAgainst IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Meeting of the Council`
`ind-b a meeting: serving` serving `, all summoned` summoned `, present` present `, for` votesFor `, against` votesAgainst MEANS
    `Meeting of the Council` WITH
        `members serving on the day of the meeting` IS `ind-b serving` serving
        `every member was duly summoned` IS summoned
        `references of the members present` IS present
        `references of the members who voted for` IS votesFor
        `references of the members who voted against` IS votesAgainst

GIVEN st IS A BOOLEAN, bud IS A BOOLEAN, sup IS A BOOLEAN, own IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Employment of a member of the Council`
`ind-b employment: State` st `, budgeted` bud `, supported` sup `, of the body represented` own MEANS
    `Employment of a member of the Council` WITH
        `a State employee` IS st
        `an employee of a budgeted body` IS bud
        `an employee of a supported body` IS sup
        `an employee of the body the member represents on the Council` IS own

GIVEN k IS A `Kinship to a member of the Council`
GIVETH A `Party in relation to a member of the Council`
`ind-b a party related only by` k MEANS
    `Party in relation to a member of the Council` WITH
        `the kinship to the member` IS k
        `the member has an interest in the financial position of the party` IS FALSE
        `the party is a corporation` IS FALSE
        `the member is an interested party in the corporation` IS FALSE
        `a family member of the member is an interested party in the corporation` IS FALSE
        `a person the member has an interest in the financial position of is an interested party in the corporation` IS FALSE
        `the party is a body` IS FALSE
        `the member manages the body or is a responsible employee in it` IS FALSE
        `a family member of the member manages the body or is a responsible employee in it` IS FALSE
        `a person the member has an interest in the financial position of manages the body or is a responsible employee in it` IS FALSE

GIVEN fin IS A BOOLEAN, corp IS A BOOLEAN, famInterested IS A BOOLEAN, isBody IS A BOOLEAN, famManages IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Party in relation to a member of the Council`
`ind-b an unrelated party: member's financial interest` fin `, a corporation` corp `with a family member interested` famInterested `, a body` isBody `managed by a family member` famManages MEANS
    `Party in relation to a member of the Council` WITH
        `the kinship to the member` IS `a relation section 29(a) does not list`
        `the member has an interest in the financial position of the party` IS fin
        `the party is a corporation` IS corp
        `the member is an interested party in the corporation` IS FALSE
        `a family member of the member is an interested party in the corporation` IS famInterested
        `a person the member has an interest in the financial position of is an interested party in the corporation` IS FALSE
        `the party is a body` IS isBody
        `the member manages the body or is a responsible employee in it` IS FALSE
        `a family member of the member manages the body or is a responsible employee in it` IS famManages
        `a person the member has an interest in the financial position of manages the body or is a responsible employee in it` IS FALSE

GIVEN conflicts IS A BOOLEAN, related IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Interest bearing on the member's function under section 29`
`ind-b the represented public's interest, conflicting` conflicts `, related to the Council's functions` related MEANS
    `Interest bearing on the member's function under section 29` WITH
        `whose interest it is` IS `the member as holder`
        `the kind of interest` IS `the interest of the public the member represents, as a kind of interest`
        `it conflicts with the performance of the member's function in the Council` IS conflicts
        `it is related to the functions of the Council` IS related

§§ `s.19 (R19-1 .. R19-9)`

-- R19-1, R19-2: the Registrar is appointed from among the Ministry's employees; publication is a duty that follows.
#ASSERT `s 19(a) — the person was appointed to hold the Registrar's powers` (`ind-b appointment: by the Minister` TRUE `, Ministry employee` TRUE `, notice published` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(a) — the person was appointed to hold the Registrar's powers` (`ind-b appointment: by the Minister` TRUE `, Ministry employee` FALSE `, notice published` TRUE)
-- R19-4, R19-5: a programme leading to a final certificate needs the Registrar's consent.
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(b) — the study programme satisfies the requirement of the Registrar's consent` (`ind-b a programme leading to a final certificate, consent given` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 19(b) — the study programme satisfies the requirement of the Registrar's consent` (`ind-b a programme leading to a final certificate, consent given` TRUE)
-- R19-6, R19-7, R19-8 (assumption: where the Council was consulted, its advice was validly given).
#ASSERT `s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` (`ind-b a foreign diploma whose scope and content match` TRUE) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` (`ind-b a foreign diploma whose scope and content match` TRUE) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` (`ind-b a foreign diploma whose scope and content match` FALSE) TRUE TRUE
-- R19-9: a recognition made conditional, the condition met, all four matters considered: it counts.
#ASSERT `s 19(c) — the foreign qualification was recognised under section 19(c)` (`ind-b a foreign diploma whose scope and content match` TRUE) `ind-b all four matters considered` TRUE TRUE

§§ `s.20 (C20-1 .. C20-5)`

#ASSERT `s 20 — the number of seats on the Council` EQUALS 11
#ASSERT `s 24, s 25(a) — the number of members of the Council under section 20` EQUALS 11
#ASSERT count `the eleven seats of the Council` EQUALS 11
#ASSERT `s 20(1) — the seat is the chair's` `seat 1: representative of the senior occupations-regulation division of the Ministry, the chair`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20(1) — the seat is the chair's` `seat 2: the Registrar`
#ASSERT elem `seat 2: the Registrar` `the eleven seats of the Council`
-- C20-5: seats 4 to 6 need the proposal of the competent Minister or Commissioner.
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` `seat 4: employee of the Ministry of Energy and Infrastructure` (`ind-b a candidate holding the position` TRUE `, proposed by the competent Minister` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` `seat 4: employee of the Ministry of Energy and Infrastructure` (`ind-b a candidate holding the position` TRUE `, proposed by the competent Minister` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` `seat 5: employee of the Ministry of Environmental Protection` (`ind-b a candidate holding the position` TRUE `, proposed by the competent Minister` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 20 — the candidate satisfies the conditions of the seat` `seat 6: employee of the National Fire and Rescue Authority` (`ind-b a candidate holding the position` TRUE `, proposed by the competent Minister` FALSE)

§§ `s.21 (C21-1 .. C21-7)`

#ASSERT `s 21 — the person is barred from appointment to the Council` (LIST (`ind-b a proceeding, unfitting` TRUE `, ending` `proceeding ended in a conviction`))
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the person is barred from appointment to the Council` (LIST (`ind-b a proceeding, unfitting` FALSE `, ending` `proceeding ended in a conviction`))
#ASSERT `s 21 — the person is barred from appointment to the Council` (LIST (`ind-b a proceeding, unfitting` TRUE `, ending` `proceeding with no final judgment yet`))
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the person is barred from appointment to the Council` (LIST (`ind-b a proceeding, unfitting` TRUE `, ending` `proceeding ended in a final judgment other than a conviction`))
#ASSERT NOT `s 21 — the person is barred from appointment to the Council` EMPTY
-- A bar under s.21 stops the appointment even to a seat whose conditions are met.
#ASSERT NOT `s 20, s 21, s 29(b) — the candidate may be appointed to the seat` `seat 11: public representative` (`ind-b a candidate holding the position` TRUE `, proposed by the competent Minister` FALSE) (LIST (`ind-b a proceeding, unfitting` TRUE `, ending` `proceeding with no final judgment yet`)) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 20, s 21, s 29(b) — the candidate may be appointed to the seat` `seat 11: public representative` (`ind-b a candidate holding the position` TRUE `, proposed by the competent Minister` FALSE) EMPTY FALSE

§§ `s.22 (C22-1 .. C22-7)`

#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office of the member in the seat` `seat 4: employee of the Ministry of Energy and Infrastructure` `appointed on the day` (YMD 2025 3 1) `, after` 0 `further terms granted` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2029 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2029 3 1) `according to` (`ind-b a record for` "s4" `in` `seat 4: employee of the Ministry of Energy and Infrastructure` `appointed 1.3.2025`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2029 3 2) `according to` (`ind-b a record for` "s4" `in` `seat 4: employee of the Ministry of Energy and Infrastructure` `appointed 1.3.2025`)
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office of the member in the seat` `seat 11: public representative` `appointed on the day` (YMD 2024 2 29) `, after` 0 `further terms granted` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2028 2 29)
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office of the member in the seat` `seat 11: public representative` `appointed on the day` (YMD 2096 2 29) `, after` 0 `further terms granted` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2100 2 28)
-- C22-4: the Registrar has no four-year term.
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office of the member in the seat` `seat 2: the Registrar` `appointed on the day` (YMD 2025 3 1) `, after` 0 `further terms granted` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22, s 23 — the member is serving on the day` (YMD 2040 1 1) `according to` (`ind-b a record for` "s2" `in` `seat 2: the Registrar` `appointed 1.3.2025`)
-- C22-6: there is no term of the Registrar's for the Minister to extend.
#ASSERT `s 22 — the Minister may extend the term of the member in the seat` `seat 2: the Registrar` "s2" EQUALS FULFILLED
-- C22-7, reading A (a further term of four years): ends 1.3.2033.  (I flagged the length as ambiguous.)
#ASSERT `s 22 — the last day of the term of office of the member in the seat` `seat 4: employee of the Ministry of Energy and Infrastructure` `appointed on the day` (YMD 2025 3 1) `, after` 1 `further terms granted` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2033 3 1)

-- C22-1 with C24, through the service records: on 1.3.2029 all eleven still serve; on 2.3.2029 only the Registrar.
#ASSERT `s 24 with ss 22 and 23 — the saving of the Council's acts applies on the day` (YMD 2029 3 1) `according to` `ind-b eleven records appointed 1.3.2025`
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 with ss 22 and 23 — the saving of the Council's acts applies on the day` (YMD 2029 3 2) `according to` `ind-b eleven records appointed 1.3.2025`
#ASSERT count (`s 22, s 23, s 20(1) — the serving members of the Council on the day` (YMD 2029 3 2) `according to` `ind-b eleven records appointed 1.3.2025`) EQUALS 1

§§ `s.23 (C23-1 .. C23-22)`

-- C23-1: resignation by a letter delivered to the Minister ends service.
#ASSERT `s 23(a) — the day the member ceased to serve under section 23(a)` `seat 8: representative of an employers' organisation` (`Events ending a member's service under section 23(a)` WITH `the day the member delivered a letter of resignation to the Minister` IS JUST (YMD 2026 5 1), `the day the member ceased to be an employee of the government ministry or a member of the body the member represents` IS NOTHING, `the day the member, a public representative, was appointed a State employee` IS NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)
-- C23-3: a ministry employee who leaves the ministry.
#ASSERT `s 23(a) — the day the member ceased to serve under section 23(a)` `seat 4: employee of the Ministry of Energy and Infrastructure` (`Events ending a member's service under section 23(a)` WITH `the day the member delivered a letter of resignation to the Minister` IS NOTHING, `the day the member ceased to be an employee of the government ministry or a member of the body the member represents` IS JUST (YMD 2026 5 1), `the day the member, a public representative, was appointed a State employee` IS NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)
-- C23-4: a representative who ceases to be a member of the body he represents.
#ASSERT `s 23(a) — the day the member ceased to serve under section 23(a)` `seat 8: representative of an employers' organisation` (`Events ending a member's service under section 23(a)` WITH `the day the member delivered a letter of resignation to the Minister` IS NOTHING, `the day the member ceased to be an employee of the government ministry or a member of the body the member represents` IS JUST (YMD 2026 5 1), `the day the member, a public representative, was appointed a State employee` IS NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)
-- C23-5: a public representative appointed a State employee.
#ASSERT `s 23(a) — the day the member ceased to serve under section 23(a)` `seat 11: public representative` (`Events ending a member's service under section 23(a)` WITH `the day the member delivered a letter of resignation to the Minister` IS NOTHING, `the day the member ceased to be an employee of the government ministry or a member of the body the member represents` IS NOTHING, `the day the member, a public representative, was appointed a State employee` IS JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 5 1)
-- C23-6: nothing happened: service continues.
#ASSERT `s 23(a) — the day the member ceased to serve under section 23(a)` `seat 11: public representative` `ind-b no events` EQUALS NOTHING

-- C23-7 .. C23-11: grounds on which the Minister must remove the member.
#ASSERT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` (`ind-b member facts: proceedings` (LIST (`ind-b a proceeding, unfitting` TRUE `, ending` `proceeding ended in a conviction`)) `, permanently unable` FALSE `, still meets the seat` TRUE `, barred by 29(b)` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` (`ind-b member facts: proceedings` (LIST (`ind-b a proceeding, unfitting` TRUE `, ending` `proceeding with no final judgment yet`)) `, permanently unable` FALSE `, still meets the seat` TRUE `, barred by 29(b)` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` (`ind-b member facts: proceedings` EMPTY `, permanently unable` TRUE `, still meets the seat` TRUE `, barred by 29(b)` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` (`ind-b member facts: proceedings` EMPTY `, permanently unable` FALSE `, still meets the seat` TRUE `, barred by 29(b)` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` (`ind-b member facts: proceedings` EMPTY `, permanently unable` FALSE `, still meets the seat` TRUE `, barred by 29(b)` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` (`ind-b member facts: proceedings` EMPTY `, permanently unable` FALSE `, still meets the seat` FALSE `, barred by 29(b)` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 23(b) — a ground for removal exists` (`ind-b member facts: proceedings` (LIST (`ind-b a proceeding, unfitting` FALSE `, ending` `proceeding ended in a conviction`)) `, permanently unable` FALSE `, still meets the seat` TRUE `, barred by 29(b)` FALSE)

-- C23-13 .. C23-21: absence (meetings monthly in 2026, removal on 1.11.2026).
-- C23-13: three in a row without justification.
#ASSERT `ind-b ground under s 23(c) on 1.11.2026 for` (LIST "A", "A", "U", "U", "U", "A", "A", "A", "A", "A")
-- C23-14: two in a row, two of ten.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b ground under s 23(c) on 1.11.2026 for` (LIST "U", "U", "A", "A", "A", "A", "A", "A", "A", "A")
-- C23-15: six of ten, never three in a row.
#ASSERT `ind-b ground under s 23(c) on 1.11.2026 for` (LIST "U", "U", "A", "U", "U", "A", "U", "U", "A", "A")
-- C23-16: five of ten is exactly half, not more than half.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b ground under s 23(c) on 1.11.2026 for` (LIST "U", "U", "A", "U", "U", "A", "U", "A", "A", "A")
-- C23-17: five of nine is more than half.
#ASSERT `ind-b ground under s 23(c) on 1.11.2026 for` (LIST "U", "U", "A", "U", "U", "A", "U", "A", "A")
-- C23-18: three in a row, all justified.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b ground under s 23(c) on 1.11.2026 for` (LIST "A", "A", "J", "J", "J", "A", "A", "A", "A", "A")
-- C23-21: six of ten absent, two of them justified, never three unjustified in a row.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b ground under s 23(c) on 1.11.2026 for` (LIST "U", "J", "A", "U", "U", "A", "J", "U", "A", "A")
-- C23-19: a ground exists but the Chair was not consulted: no power.
#ASSERT `s 23(c) — the Minister may remove the member for absence` "s8" (`ind-b meetings of 2026 from month` 1 `coded` (LIST "A", "A", "U", "U", "U", "A", "A", "A", "A", "A")) (YMD 2026 11 1) FALSE EQUALS FULFILLED
-- No ground at all: no power even with the Chair consulted.
#ASSERT `s 23(c) — the Minister may remove the member for absence` "s8" (`ind-b meetings of 2026 from month` 1 `coded` (LIST "U", "U", "A", "A", "A", "A", "A", "A", "A", "A")) (YMD 2026 11 1) TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED

§§ `s.24 (C24-1 .. C24-5)`

#ASSERT `s 24 — the saving of the Council's acts applies` (`ind-b serving` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6"))
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 — the saving of the Council's acts applies` (`ind-b serving` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5"))
#ASSERT NOT `s 24 — the saving of the Council's acts applies` (`ind-b serving` (LIST "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6", "m7"))
#ASSERT `s 24 — the saving of the Council's acts applies` (`ind-b serving` `ind-b all eleven`)
#ASSERT `s 24 — the saving of the Council's acts applies` (`ind-b serving` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6", "m7"))

§§ `s.25 (C25-1 .. C25-16)`

-- C25-1 .. C25-5: the quorum is six of the eleven, the Chair among them.
#ASSERT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6") `, for` EMPTY `, against` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5") `, for` EMPTY `, against` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6", "m7") `, for` EMPTY `, against` EMPTY)
#ASSERT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` `ind-b all eleven` `, for` EMPTY `, against` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6", "m7", "m8", "m9") `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5") `, for` EMPTY `, against` EMPTY)

-- C25-6 .. C25-10: a majority of those taking part and voting; on a tie the Chair's vote decides.
#ASSERT `s 25(b) — the votes carry the proposal at` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6", "m7") `, for` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4") `, against` (LIST "m5", "m6", "m7"))
#ASSERT `s 25(b) — the votes carry the proposal at` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6") `, for` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3") `, against` (LIST "m4", "m5", "m6"))
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(b) — the votes carry the proposal at` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6") `, for` (LIST "m2", "m3", "m4") `, against` (LIST "m1", "m5", "m6"))
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(b) — the votes carry the proposal at` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6", "m7") `, for` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3") `, against` (LIST "m4", "m5", "m6", "m7"))
#ASSERT `s 25(b) — the votes carry the proposal at` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6", "m7") `, for` (LIST "m2", "m3", "m4") `, against` (LIST "m5", "m6"))
#ASSERT `s 25(a), (b) — the Council's decision is carried at the meeting` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6", "m7") `, for` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4") `, against` (LIST "m5", "m6", "m7"))
-- C25-11: a tie with the Chair present and not voting: the text does not answer.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 25(b) — the votes carry the proposal at` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6") `, for` (LIST "m2", "m3") `, against` (LIST "m4", "m5"))

-- C25-12 .. C25-14: discussion in an incomplete composition: all summoned and the Chair present.
#ASSERT `s 25(c) — the Council may deliberate in an incomplete composition` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3") `, for` EMPTY `, against` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(c) — the Council may deliberate in an incomplete composition` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` FALSE `, present` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3") `, for` EMPTY `, against` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(c) — the Council may deliberate in an incomplete composition` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6", "m7", "m8", "m9") `, for` EMPTY `, against` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a) — the meeting has a quorum` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m2", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6", "m7", "m8", "m9") `, for` EMPTY `, against` EMPTY)
-- C25-15, one of my two readings ((c) permits discussion only): three present cannot carry a decision.
#ASSERT NOT `s 25(a), (b) — the Council's decision is carried at the meeting` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3") `, for` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3") `, against` EMPTY)
-- ... and the other reading is callable: the same sitting decides under it.
#ASSERT `s 25(c), alternative reading — the Council's decision is carried at a meeting held in an incomplete composition` (`ind-b a meeting: serving` `ind-b all eleven` `, all summoned` TRUE `, present` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3") `, for` (LIST "m1", "m2", "m3") `, against` EMPTY)

§§ `s.26 (C26-1 .. C26-3)`

#ASSERT `s 26(b) — the Council may delegate its powers in the function to a subcommittee` `function (3): advising the Registrar on individual applications and decisions`
#ASSERT NOT `s 26(b) — the Council may delegate its powers in the function to a subcommittee` `function (2): advising the Registrar on the Ministry's policy`
#ASSERT NOT `s 26(b) — the Council may delegate its powers in the function to a subcommittee` `function (1): advising the Minister on exemption from licensing`
#ASSERT `s 26(b) — the Council's power to delegate its powers in the function to the subcommittee` `function (2): advising the Registrar on the Ministry's policy` "a policy subcommittee" EQUALS FULFILLED

§§ `s.27 (C27-1 .. C27-6)`

-- C27-1: a self-employed public representative: no payment for meetings, travel refunded.
#ASSERT NOT `s 27(a) — the member is entitled to payment from the Ministry for taking part in meetings` (`ind-b employment: State` FALSE `, budgeted` FALSE `, supported` FALSE `, of the body represented` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 27 — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses` (`ind-b employment: State` FALSE `, budgeted` FALSE `, supported` FALSE `, of the body represented` FALSE)
-- C27-2, C27-3: State and budgeted-body employees: no refund.
#ASSERT NOT `s 27 — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses` (`ind-b employment: State` TRUE `, budgeted` FALSE `, supported` FALSE `, of the body represented` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 27 — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses` (`ind-b employment: State` FALSE `, budgeted` TRUE `, supported` FALSE `, of the body represented` FALSE)
-- C27-5: employed by the very body he represents: (b) carves him out of (a).
#ASSERT NOT `s 27 — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses` (`ind-b employment: State` FALSE `, budgeted` FALSE `, supported` FALSE `, of the body represented` TRUE)
-- C27-6: employed by an unrelated private firm.
#ASSERT `s 27 — the member is entitled to a refund of reasonable travel expenses` (`ind-b employment: State` FALSE `, budgeted` FALSE `, supported` FALSE `, of the body represented` FALSE)

§§ `s.28 (C28-1)`

-- Assumption: the act is the member's act in the Council and, for items 2, 4 and 5, the provision is one the item names.
#ASSERT `s 28 — the member with the employment` (`ind-b employment: State` FALSE `, budgeted` FALSE `, supported` FALSE `, of the body represented` FALSE) `is treated as a State employee under` `the Public Service (Gifts) Law 1979` `for an act in the Council being` TRUE `and a provision the item names being` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28 — the member with the employment` (`ind-b employment: State` FALSE `, budgeted` FALSE `, supported` FALSE `, of the body represented` FALSE) `is treated as a State employee under` `the Penal Law, the provisions concerning public servants` `for an act in the Council being` TRUE `and a provision the item names being` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28 — the member with the employment` (`ind-b employment: State` FALSE `, budgeted` FALSE `, supported` FALSE `, of the body represented` FALSE) `is treated as a State employee under` `the Public Service (Restrictions after Retirement) Law 1969` `for an act in the Council being` TRUE `and a provision the item names being` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28 — the member with the employment` (`ind-b employment: State` FALSE `, budgeted` FALSE `, supported` FALSE `, of the body represented` FALSE) `is treated as a State employee under` `the Civil Service (Restriction of Party Activity and Fund-raising) Law 1959, the provisions on all State employees` `for an act in the Council being` TRUE `and a provision the item names being` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28 — the member with the employment` (`ind-b employment: State` FALSE `, budgeted` FALSE `, supported` FALSE `, of the body represented` FALSE) `is treated as a State employee under` `the Evidence Ordinance, the provisions on a public servant's certificate` `for an act in the Council being` TRUE `and a provision the item names being` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28 — the member with the employment` (`ind-b employment: State` FALSE `, budgeted` FALSE `, supported` FALSE `, of the body represented` FALSE) `is treated as a State employee under` `the Knesset Elections Law` `for an act in the Council being` TRUE `and a provision the item names being` TRUE

§§ `s.29 (C29-1 .. C29-8 and the definitions)`

-- "Family member": the thirteen relations the definition lists (step-relations included), and one it does not.
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a spouse of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a parent of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a parent of a parent of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a child of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a spouse of a child of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a brother or sister of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a child of a brother or sister of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a brother-in-law or sister-in-law of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `an uncle or aunt of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a child of an uncle or aunt of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a parent of a spouse of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a grandchild of the member`
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a relation section 29(a) does not list`
-- "Relative": a family member; (2) a person in whose finances the member has an interest; (3) a corporation in
-- which a family member is an interested party; (4) a body a family member manages; not a friend's corporation.
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5 — the party is a relative of the member` (`ind-b a party related only by` `a brother or sister of the member`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.5 — the party is a relative of the member` (`ind-b a party related only by` `a relation section 29(a) does not list`)
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5 — the party is a relative of the member` (`ind-b an unrelated party: member's financial interest` TRUE `, a corporation` FALSE `with a family member interested` FALSE `, a body` FALSE `managed by a family member` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5 — the party is a relative of the member` (`ind-b an unrelated party: member's financial interest` FALSE `, a corporation` TRUE `with a family member interested` TRUE `, a body` FALSE `managed by a family member` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5 — the party is a relative of the member` (`ind-b an unrelated party: member's financial interest` FALSE `, a corporation` FALSE `with a family member interested` FALSE `, a body` TRUE `managed by a family member` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.5 — the party is a relative of the member` (`ind-b an unrelated party: member's financial interest` FALSE `, a corporation` TRUE `with a family member interested` FALSE `, a body` FALSE `managed by a family member` FALSE)

-- C29-1, C29-2: barred only by a regular conflict that prevents the core of the function.
#ASSERT `s 29(b) — the person is barred from the Council by regular conflicts of interest` TRUE `with the main part of the function prevented being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(b) — the person is barred from the Council by regular conflicts of interest` TRUE `with the main part of the function prevented being` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(b) — the person is barred from the Council by regular conflicts of interest` FALSE `with the main part of the function prevented being` TRUE

-- C29-5: seat 8 weighing the employers' interests, related to the Council's functions: not a conflict for that alone.
#ASSERT NOT `s 29 with s 20 — the member in the seat` `seat 8: representative of an employers' organisation` `is in a conflict of interest among the interests` (LIST (`ind-b the represented public's interest, conflicting` TRUE `, related to the Council's functions` TRUE))
-- C29-6: seat 3 has no (e): the same interest is a conflict.
#ASSERT `s 29 with s 20 — the member in the seat` `seat 3: the Commissioner for Standards, or an employee on the Commissioner's behalf` `is in a conflict of interest among the interests` (LIST (`ind-b the represented public's interest, conflicting` TRUE `, related to the Council's functions` TRUE))
-- C29-7: seat 8, an interest unrelated to the Council's functions: (e) does not protect.
#ASSERT `s 29 with s 20 — the member in the seat` `seat 8: representative of an employers' organisation` `is in a conflict of interest among the interests` (LIST (`ind-b the represented public's interest, conflicting` TRUE `, related to the Council's functions` FALSE))
-- C29-8: seat 8, the brother's company would benefit: a relative's personal interest is a conflict.
#ASSERT `s 29 with s 20 — the member in the seat` `seat 8: representative of an employers' organisation` `is in a conflict of interest among the interests` (LIST (`Interest bearing on the member's function under section 29` WITH `whose interest it is` IS `someone else as holder` (`ind-b a party related only by` `a brother or sister of the member`), `the kind of interest` IS `a personal interest of the holder`, `it conflicts with the performance of the member's function in the Council` IS TRUE, `it is related to the functions of the Council` IS TRUE))
-- (e) is for seats 7 to 11 only.
#ASSERT `s 20, s 29(e) — the seat is one of the seats 7 to 11` `seat 7: representative of the workers' organisation with the most licence holders`
#ASSERT `s 20, s 29(e) — the seat is one of the seats 7 to 11` `seat 11: public representative`
#ASSERT NOT `s 20, s 29(e) — the seat is one of the seats 7 to 11` `seat 6: employee of the National Fire and Rescue Authority`
#ASSERT `s 29(e) — a member who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` FALSE `may take into account the interests of the public the member represents, which are related to the Council's functions:` TRUE EQUALS FULFILLED
